fstdumper patch: attribution and license notice

Upstream project: fstdumper, https://github.com/semify-eda/fstdumper
Upstream revision: 3c7506333d2c9ad098d4526209621ea401a077ba

Patch in this repository (third_party/fstdumper/):

fstdumper-xcelium.patch
   Makes fstdumper work on Cadence Xcelium. Builds for Icarus Verilog keep
   the upstream behaviour. Key changes:
   - scopes: traverse interfaces; reach generate blocks, instance arrays,
     named begin/fork, static task/function variables and clocking blocks
     through vpiInternalScope;
   - types: dump enum, packed struct/union, packed arrays, bit and integer
     nets and clocking-block signals; count objects FST cannot hold and
     report them in one line per $dumpvars;
   - data: declare each signal once; write port-collapsed nets as FST
     aliases; skip no-op value changes; flush pending value changes before
     $finish;
   - names: write escaped identifiers and names containing '$' as in the
     RTL; write declared ranges, port directions and interface definition
     names;
   - robustness: skip protected (encrypted) objects and objects without
     read access; guard NULL names, unusable sizes and over-long names;
     handle vpiNamedEvent without vpi_get_value; fix a one byte buffer
     overrun when dumping X values.

   Files: src/sys_fst.c and src/vcd_priv.c (modified), src/fst_sv_vpi.h
   (new).

